n    31→        \"quote\": \"If you go full auto, there will be collateral damage. Users trust Claude Code because it asks before doing anything.\",\n    32→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    33→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    34→      },\n    35→      {\n    36→        \"quote\": \"As of today, that classifier overhead no longer counts toward your usage limits on Pro, Max, and Team plans.\",\n    37→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    38→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n    39→      },\n    40→      {\n    41→        \"quote\": \"Claude found their personal financial ledger elsewhere on their hard drive when working on nonprofit books, calling it 'a bit of an overreach.'\",\n    42→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    43→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    44→      }\n    45→    ]\n    46→  },\n    47→  {\n    48→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    49→    \"title\": \"Session-to-Session Messaging\",\n    50→    \"description\": \"Claude Code sessions can now message each other using the ListAgents tool and SendMessage. Claude can communicate between sessions without re-explaining context when a change in one session affects what another is working on. Available on macOS and Linux, requires v2.1.224 or later.\",\n    51→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    52→    \"url\": \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w32\",\n    53→    \"date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n    54→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    55→  },\n    56→  {\n    57→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    58→    \"title\": \"Self-Hosted Environments (Public Beta)\",\n    59→    \"description\": \"Team and Enterprise plans can now run Claude Code cloud sessions on their organization's own infrastructure. Run `claude self-hosted-runner` on machines or containers to turn them into runners. Sessions run inside your network with access to internal services.\",\n    60→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n    61→    \"url\": \"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new/2026-w32\",\n    62→    \"date\": \"2026-08-03\",\n    63→    \"community_feedback\": []\n    64→  },\n    65→  {\n    66→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n    67→    \"title\": \"Weekly Limits Promotion Extended Through August 31\",\n    68→    \"description\": \"Claude Code extended its 50% higher weekly limits promotion through August 31, 2026 for Pro, Max, Team, and seat-based Enterprise users. Originally set to end August 19, the extension comes as users reported frustration with rapid usage depletion and outages.\",\n    69→    \"updateType\": \"announcement\",\n    70→    \"url\": \"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49348751\",\n    71→    \"date\": \"2026-08-19\",\n    72→    \"community_feedback\": [\n    73→      {\n    74→        \"quote\": \"Between the outages and just overall crap utility of Opus/Fable lately, I was considering canceling my subscription.\",\n    75→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    76→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    77→      },\n    78→      {\n    79→        \"quote\": \"With ultracode active, multiple agents ate my $100 credit in no time flat while producing nothing useful.\",\n    80→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    81→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    82→      },\n    83→      {\n    84→        \"quote\": \"I made the full switch to 5.6 sol and Codex about a month ago. Better experience, higher limits and better output than Opus 4.8. Almost 0 switching cost - just rename your Claude.md to agents.md.\",\n    85→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    86→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    87→      },\n    88→      {\n    89→        \"quote\": \"OpenAI weekly limits feel infinite compared to Anthropic's.\",\n    90→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    91→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    92→      },\n    93→      {\n    94→        \"quote\": \"I'm 100% convinced that its verbose writing style is to generate tokens to make you hit your limit quicker.\",\n    95→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n    96→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n    97→      },\n    98→      {\n    99→        \"quote\": \"Anthropic has been struggling all of 2026 with usage limits and shenanigans around 'peak hour' reduction.\",\n   100→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   101→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   102→      },\n   103→      {\n   104→        \"quote\": \"The race is actually between locally optimized rigs with extremely strict context management, and the rest.\",\n   105→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   106→        \"sentiment\": \"neutral\"\n   107→      }\n   108→    ]\n   109→  },\n   110→  {\n   111→    \"productName\": \"Claude Code\",\n   112→    \"title\": \"Skill and Plugin Security Scanning (Beta)\",\n   113→    \"description\": \"Enterprise plans can now enable automatic security scanning for third-party skills and plugins when uploaded or edited. Helps detect malicious content before deployment.\",\n   114→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   115→    \"url\": \"https://support.claude.com/en/articles/12138966-release-notes\",\n   116→    \"date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   117→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   118→  },\n   119→  {\n   120→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   121→    \"title\": \"Origin Code Hosting Platform Launch\",\n   122→    \"description\": \"Cursor launched Origin, a new Git hosting platform in early beta for paid plans. Features include hosted codebases with GitHub repo syncing, pull requests with two-way sync, agent integration for code analysis, and app extensions for Vercel, Depot, and Buildkite. Launch coincided with GitHub's 7-hour outage on August 17.\",\n   123→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   124→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   125→    \"date\": \"2026-08-17\",\n   126→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   127→      {\n   128→        \"quote\": \"It's like going from bad to worse.\",\n   129→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   130→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   131→      },\n   132→      {\n   133→        \"quote\": \"They are doing the easiest part of git hosting and don't even support GitHub Actions yet.\",\n   134→        \"source\": \"HN\",\n   135→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   136→      }\n   137→    ]\n   138→  },\n   139→  {\n   140→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   141→    \"title\": \"Cloud Agents with Subscriptions and Custom Modes\",\n   142→    \"description\": \"Cloud agents gained autonomous capabilities to monitor PRs, watch Slack threads, and run scheduled tasks. New features include custom modes with pinned skills, subagents on isolated VMs, /goal command for persistent objectives, and non-interruptive steering for guiding agents.\",\n   143→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   144→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   145→    \"date\": \"2026-08-19\",\n   146→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   147→  },\n   148→  {\n   149→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   150→    \"title\": \"Grok 4.6 Model Release\",\n   151→    \"description\": \"Cursor released Grok 4.6, a new model focused on long-running agents and complex coding tasks. Features include 500K context window, new XHigh reasoning capability, and improved multi-step reasoning with self-checking. Pricing maintained at $2/$6.\",\n   152→    \"updateType\": \"release\",\n   153→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/blog/grok-4-6\",\n   154→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   155→    \"community_feedback\": [\n   156→      {\n   157→        \"quote\": \"Users reported impressive value overall and strong performance on coding and knowledge tasks.\",\n   158→        \"source\": \"Cursor Forum\",\n   159→        \"sentiment\": \"positive\"\n   160→      },\n   161→      {\n   162→        \"quote\": \"Some users reported bad experiences with the model not solving problems and high token consumption (>15% usage in a single day).\",\n   163→        \"source\": \"Cursor Forum\",\n   164→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   165→      },\n   166→      {\n   167→        \"quote\": \"Issues with auto-overriding without user approval.\",\n   168→        \"source\": \"Cursor Forum\",\n   169→        \"sentiment\": \"negative\"\n   170→      }\n   171→    ]\n   172→  },\n   173→  {\n   174→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   175→    \"title\": \"Cloud Agents 3x Faster Startup with Builds\",\n   176→    \"description\": \"Background preparation of development environments reduces startup time to 3x faster. Agents boot from cached environments with cloned repos and installed dependencies. Failed builds don't disrupt operations as agents continue using last successful build.\",\n   177→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   178→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   179→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   180→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   181→  },\n   182→  {\n   183→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   184→    \"title\": \"Google Workspace Plugins\",\n   185→    \"description\": \"New plugins enable agents to work across Gmail (search, draft, send), Google Drive (files, folders), and Google Calendar (events, scheduling). Provides direct integration for workflow automation.\",\n   186→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   187→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   188→    \"date\": \"2026-08-04\",\n   189→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   190→  },\n   191→  {\n   192→    \"productName\": \"Cursor\",\n   193→    \"title\": \"Cursor Router with Auto Intelligence\",\n   194→    \"description\": \"Cursor Router optimizes model selection with Auto Intelligence and Auto Balance, delivering 68% lower costs for Intelligence mode while maintaining higher satisfaction.\",\n   195→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   196→    \"url\": \"https://cursor.com/changelog\",\n   197→    \"date\": \"2026-08-06\",\n   198→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   199→  },\n   200→  {\n   201→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   202→    \"title\": \"Agent Plugins 1.0 Launch\",\n   203→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot launched Agent Plugins 1.0 for VS Code, CLI, and the app, enabling portable agent plugins with multi-catalog search. Features include automatic approval via flags, Cursor skill import and sync, and MCP 2026-07-28 protocol support.\",\n   204→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   205→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   206→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   207→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   208→  },\n   209→  {\n   210→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   211→    \"title\": \"Grok 4.6 Model Integration\",\n   212→    \"description\": \"GitHub Copilot integrated Grok 4.6 model, expanding model choices for users. The model is designed for long-running agents and complex coding tasks with improved multi-step reasoning.\",\n   213→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   214→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   215→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   216→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   217→  },\n   218→  {\n   219→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   220→    \"title\": \"Code Review Effort Levels GA\",\n   221→    \"description\": \"Code review effort levels became generally available, providing more granular control over automated code review capabilities. Allows teams to customize review depth and automation.\",\n   222→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   223→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   224→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   225→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   226→  },\n   227→  {\n   228→    \"productName\": \"GitHub Copilot\",\n   229→    \"title\": \"Usage Metrics API Expansion\",\n   230→    \"description\": \"Usage metrics API expanded to include agent app activity, providing more detailed insights into how teams are using Copilot across different platforms and workflows.\",\n   231→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   232→    \"url\": \"https://github.blog/changelog/label/copilot/\",\n   233→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   234→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   235→  },\n   236→  {\n   237→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   238→    \"title\": \"Devin Coach Suggestions\",\n   239→    \"description\": \"Devin introduced real-time prompt improvement suggestions that surface directly in the session input box, helping users formulate better prompts and improve AI interactions.\",\n   240→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   241→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   242→    \"date\": \"2026-08-14\",\n   243→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   244→  },\n   245→  {\n   246→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   247→    \"title\": \"Side Chats Feature\",\n   248→    \"description\": \"Users can now start conversations anchored to any point in a session to ask questions without interrupting Devin's main work flow, enabling parallel exploration and clarification.\",\n   249→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   250→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   251→    \"date\": \"2026-08-12\",\n   252→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   253→  },\n   254→  {\n   255→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   256→    \"title\": \"Automations Queueing Support\",\n   257→    \"description\": \"Automations now support queueing with configurable maximum concurrent runs and queue depth. Users can view queue lifecycle states and manage execution flow more effectively.\",\n   258→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   259→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   260→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   261→    \"community_feedback\": []\n   262→  },\n   263→  {\n   264→    \"productName\": \"Devin\",\n   265→    \"title\": \"Security Profiles GA\",\n   266→    \"description\": \"Security profiles became generally available, allowing admins to define profiles governing network access across sessions and automations for improved security control.\",\n   267→    \"updateType\": \"feature\",\n   268→    \"url\": \"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/overview\",\n   269→    \"date\": \"2026-08-07\",\n   270→    \"community_feedback\": []\